  "notes": "Two claims in the research do the work here, and they pull in opposite directions from the other Roc-A-Fella entries. First, \"drums sit behind the loop rather than over it\" — authored as `velocityTiers.main` 68–82, the lowest main tier in this batch, so the kit is present but never the loudest thing. Second, \"4-bar loops with real motion\" — i–iv–VII and ii–V–i, which is genuine functional harmony rather than a two-chord vamp, so `extensions.ninth` is 0.2 and the voicing is open for the organ and choir stacks. The replayed organ-pedal bass following the changes is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.62: it tracks the progression but is not welded to the kick. ⚠ ii–V–i is written with a major V, as the research writes it, with `borrowed.V` raised to 0.35 so the raised leading tone actually appears. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this medium-high, and the inferred parameters are the drum numbers — the entry documents the Roc-A-Fella idiom *via its producers*, so the ghost placement and hat density are Bink!/Just Blaze-camp norms rather than a per-record reading. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 45 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
